course: dictionary
lesson: 857
title: The prefix bi- means two
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A prefix is a small group of letters at the start of a word. It changes the meaning of the word. Bi- is a prefix that means two, or twice. When you see bi at the start of a word, look for the idea of two.
explain: «That is the way all Bi-Coloured-Python-Rock-Snakes always talk.» Bi-coloured means two-coloured. The snake has two colours, and bi- tells you the number is two.
explain: Use the prefix to guess the meaning of a new word. Bicycle has two wheels. Bilingual means two languages. Biannual means twice a year. Once you know bi- means two, you can work out many words without a dictionary.
fact: Bi- means two or twice.
fact: A bicycle has two wheels, and bilingual means speaking two languages.
fact: Biannual means twice a year, and biped means an animal with two feet.
fact: Bisect means to cut into two equal parts.
fact: Binary is a number system based on two.
exercise: What does bi- mean at the start of a word? | Before | *Two or twice | Under | Three
exercise: How many wheels does a bicycle have? | One | Three | Four | *Two
exercise: A bilingual child speaks how many languages? | One | Four | *Two | Three
test: A biannual event happens how often? | *Twice a year | Once a day | Every ten years | Once a week
test: What is a biped? | A bird | An animal with four legs | *An animal with two feet | A fish
exam: Which word means to cut into two equal parts? | Binary | *Bisect | Biped | Bicycle
